        "original_id": "75e0549f-d747-5450-8138-17f5489b4da8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Markus Feehily, Bobby Fuller, Randy Fuller\n- Music Groups: Westlife, The Bobby Fuller Four\n- Albums: Fire\n- Topics: singers, songwriters, rock music\n\nFacts:\n- Bobby Fuller was born on October 22, 1942, and he died on July 18, 1966.\n- Bobby Fuller was an American rock singer, songwriter, and guitarist.\n- Bobby Fuller was best known for “Love's Made a Fool of You” and for his cover of “I Fought the Law,” recorded with The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Randy Fuller was born on January 29, 1944.\n- Randy Fuller is an American rock singer, songwriter, and bass player.\n- Randy Fuller was best known for performing with his older brother Bobby Fuller in the 1960s rock group The Bobby Fuller Four.\n- Markus Feehily was born on 28 May 1980.\n- Markus Feehily, formerly known as Mark Feehily, is an Irish singer and songwriter.\n- Fire is the debut solo studio album by Markus Feehily.\n- Markus Feehily was a vocalist in Westlife before releasing Fire.",
